<title>BULGARIA: FRANCE GRANTS BULGARIA 5,000T WHEAT.</title>
<headline>FRANCE GRANTS BULGARIA 5,000T WHEAT.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>France has agreed to grant Bulgaria 5,000 tonnes of wheat to alleviate shortages in the Balkan country, state news agency BTA said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the French ambassador to Sofia and the agriculture minister would sign a formal agreement on Tuesday and the grain was expected to arrive at Bourgas port within 20 days.</p>
<p>Excessive Bulgarian wheat exports in 1995 coupled with a poor harvest last year led to shortages intensified by a cash crisis for the caretaker cabinet. -- Sofia Newsroom +359-2 91188</p>
